  "validationNotes": [
    "The user supplied the Panchang's printed explanatory legend: planetary rise/set and Sun/Moon/planetary sign-change times are in IST hour-minute; tithi/nakshatra/yoga/karana are separately shown in ghadi-pala and clock time.",
    "The legend's example uses clock values 26:31 and 28:53 for events before the following sunrise, supporting the conventional after-midnight notation for values above 24. Raw strings remain authoritative.",
    "Do not infer missing directions for Jupiter or Agastya.",
    "The two Panchang centers are not Pithoragarh. Compare only after evaluating location-specific calculations at the stated source coordinates, and keep provider coordinate uncertainty visible.",
    "Some reported labels/directions may appear counterintuitive. Preserve them verbatim rather than silently correcting.",
    "Drik Panchang data transcribed by the user on 2026-11-15; all supplied times are preserved as local IST clock times. Reported total durations are not independently recalculated and are not stored as event times.",
    "Drik Almora and Ramnagar exact coordinates as selected in the Drik interface were not supplied. The Ganesh Martand/Tara Prasad coordinates are location metadata only, not asserted Drik coordinates.",
    "For Drik Jupiter/Venus intervals, 'अस्त समाप्त' is stored as the supplied end of the Asta interval; it should not be silently relabeled as independently verified heliacal rising.",
    "Agastya Arghya date/time and the separately stated Agastya star rise/set moments are distinct observations. Preserve that distinction; do not treat Arghya start as a geometric rise instant.",
    "The source text's weekday labels and some reported duration totals may be inconsistent with Gregorian calendar arithmetic; the ISO dates and raw clock times are stored as supplied and should be checked against source screenshots before publication."
